## Fit Mode (applies uniformly across ALL media types above)

```css
.bg-container[data-fit="fill"]    { object-fit: cover;    background-size: cover; }
.bg-container[data-fit="fit"]     { object-fit: contain;  background-size: contain; background-color: var(--bg-primary); }
.bg-container[data-fit="stretch"] { object-fit: fill;     background-size: 100% 100%; }
.bg-container[data-fit="center"]  { object-fit: none;     background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat; }
.bg-container[data-fit="tile"]    { background-repeat: repeat; background-size: auto; }
```
For video/canvas-based sources, `object-fit`/`object-position` are 
applied directly to the element; for CSS `background-image` sources, 
the equivalent `background-size`/`background-position` pair is used — 
the Fit Mode selector UI (see Background Shower prompt below) is 
agnostic to which underlying property gets set.

## Format Detection & Adapter Selection

```js
function selectAdapter(fileOrUrl) {
  const ext = getExtension(fileOrUrl).toLowerCase();
  if (['mp4','webm','mov'].includes(ext)) return new VideoSource(fileOrUrl);
  if (ext === 'gif') return new AnimatedGifSource(fileOrUrl);
  if (ext === 'svg') return isSvgAnimated(fileOrUrl) 
    ? new AnimatedSvgSource(fileOrUrl) : new ImageSource(fileOrUrl);
  if (['jpg','jpeg','png','webp','avif'].includes(ext)) return new ImageSource(fileOrUrl);
  throw new Error(`Unsupported background format: ${ext}`);
}
```
`isSvgAnimated()` checks the SVG's markup for `<animate>`, `<animateTransform>`, 
or a `<style>` block containing `@keyframes`/`animation:` — a plain 
static SVG icon should never be routed through the animated adapter's 
extra overhead.

## Performance & Battery Guardrails

- Only ONE `BackgroundSource` is ever mounted per visible surface — 
  switching wallpapers calls `unmount()` on the old source before 
  `mount()` on the new one, never runs two simultaneously (even during 
  a crossfade transition, both old and new sources render to two 
  stacked layers but the OLD one calls `pause()` immediately once its 
  fade-out completes, not left silently running underneath).
- Low-Power Mode (wired from Settings #90) calls `.pause()` on any 
  `isAnimated() === true` source system-wide and swaps to its 
  `getPosterFrame()` result — this must work identically whether the 
  source is a video, GIF, animated SVG, or live scene, which is exactly 
  why the unified interface exists.
- Any background not currently visible (e.g. a background sitting on a 
  non-active Space) is paused, not unmounted — resuming a Space via 
  Spaces (#52) navigation should feel instant, not require re-decoding 
  media from scratch.

