## Prompt — Background Shower (Full-Screen Preview + Controls)

```
Design the "Background Shower" — a full-viewport preview surface for 
Roboticela OS's Wallpaper & Screen Saver Settings page (#82), letting 
the user see and configure a background exactly as it will render on 
the real Desktop, with every fit mode and playback behavior live-
adjustable before applying.

## Layout

Full-bleed within the Settings detail pane (not literally full 
viewport — respects the Settings Shell's content area, but stretches 
to fill 100% of that area's available space, min-height 480px), 16px 
radius, `overflow: hidden`, 1px `--border-default`.

- The background media itself renders via the Universal Background 
  Engine (mounted directly into this preview container, same adapter 
  code path the real Desktop uses — this is a live instance, not a 
  static screenshot).
- Overlay chrome (toolbar): floats at the bottom of the preview, 
  `rgba(0,0,0,0.4)` scrim strip, `backdrop-filter: blur(16px)`, full 
  width, 56px height, flex row, `--space-4` padding, items described 
  below.

## Fit Mode Selector

Segmented Control (#27, icon-only variant), 5 options: Fill / Fit / 
Stretch / Center / Tile — each icon a small pictogram illustrating the 
mode (e.g. Fill = a frame with content bleeding past edges, Fit = 
content fully inside with letterbox bars). Selecting instantly calls 
`source.setFitMode(mode)` on the live-mounted background — no separate 
"preview" vs. "apply" step, what you see IS what gets set.

## Behavior Mode Row

Segmented Control (#27, text+icon variant), 2 options:
- **Single Image**: the currently selected background renders as one 
  static (or looping, if animated) source — no rotation.
- **Slideshow**: enables a secondary control row (slides down/fades in 
  below, `var(--duration-base)`):
  - Thumbnail strip of all images in the selected slideshow folder/set 
    (reuses the horizontal scroll-snap filmstrip pattern from Gallery 
    View #74), each Thumbnail Preview Tile (#47) with a small drag-
    handle for manual reordering.
  - Interval Stepper (#26) — "Change every: [5 min / 15 min / 1 hour / 
    1 day]" as a Dropdown (#37) rather than freeform numeric entry.
  - Shuffle Toggle Switch (#21).

## Playback Control (only visible/enabled when the current source's 
`isAnimated()` returns true — video, animated GIF, animated SVG, or 
live scene)

- Play/Pause icon-Button (#20, icon-only) — toggles `source.pause()`/ 
  `source.resume()` on the live preview directly. Icon swaps between 
  play-triangle and pause-bars glyphs based on current state (not two 
  separate buttons).
- Small scrubber (reuses Progress Bar #18's track styling but draggable 
  like a Slider #25) for video sources specifically — shows playback 
  position, draggable to seek. Hidden entirely for GIF/SVG/live-scene 
  sources where "seeking" isn't a meaningful concept, only Play/Pause 
  applies to those.
- "Reduce Motion respects this setting" hint text (12px, `--text-
  tertiary`) appears beneath the playback controls if the system's 
  Reduce Motion accessibility setting (#92) is currently ON — 
  clarifies to the user why the background might already be paused by 
  default regardless of this control.

## Apply / Cancel

Bottom-right of the toolbar (separated by a flexible spacer from the 
controls above): "Cancel" secondary Button (#20) reverts the preview 
to whatever was actually active before this session opened (calls 
`unmount()` on the preview instance, no changes persisted), "Set as 
Wallpaper" primary Button commits the current preview configuration 
(source + fit mode + behavior mode + slideshow config) as the real 
Desktop background for the active Space, via the same `mount()` call 
now targeting the actual Desktop Surface (#71) container instead of 
this preview.

## Guardrails

- The preview MUST use the real Universal Background Engine adapters — 
  never a simplified/faked preview renderer — so what the user 
  configures here is guaranteed identical to the real result, with 
  zero "it looked different once applied" surprises.
- Fit Mode and Behavior Mode changes apply live/instantly to the 
  preview; only the final source+config commit is gated behind the 
  explicit "Set as Wallpaper" action — don't require a separate 
  "Preview" button before showing changes.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` → any animated source in the preview 
  mounts already paused at its poster frame by default (matching how 
  it would actually behave on the real Desktop under that setting), 
  Play/Pause remains manually available so the user can still preview 
  the motion deliberately if they choose to.
```